# VitePress build output and its dev cache. The GENERATED PAGES under
# components/ are deliberately NOT ignored: they are committed generated truth,
# the same as packages/core/docs/llms.txt and component-meta.json, so a change to
# what the site publishes shows up in a diff and `yarn validate:docs-pages`
# has a committed output to compare a fresh render against. TASK-N2-A3's finding
# F-4 is exactly the failure of git-ignoring a generated document a consumer reads.
.vitepress/dist/
.vitepress/cache/

# TASK-N2-D3. The playground sandbox assets are BUILD OUTPUT copied from
# apps/storybook/public/playground (the single producer), regenerated from
# current source on every build, and git-ignored there for the same reason.
# public/playground/seeds.json is deliberately NOT ignored: it is generated
# truth written by `yarn generate:docs-pages`, and `yarn validate:docs-pages`
# needs a committed copy to compare a fresh render against.
public/playground/dzup-core.mjs
public/playground/tokens.css
public/playground/core.css
public/playground/repl/
